  "status": "HARVESTED, NOT YET SERVED (#800). Verbatim table; no join to catalog stats and no solver wiring.",
  "note": "Wiki-harvested seed shard for Essence Crafting COMBINED PREFIX shards - one shard that grants TWO effects into the single prefix slot. Distinct from `essence_crafting.json` placements (table 1b), which are keyed by one effect. Verbatim from the DDO wiki: names, effect pairs, slot lists and crafting levels exactly as printed, including the page's own typos.",
  "sources": {
   "recipes": "https://ddowiki.com/page/Essence_Crafting",
   "section": "Combined prefixes - Expand Dual Shard Recipe List"
  },
  "evidence": "docs/wiki-evidence/essence-crafting.md",
  "harvested": "2026-09-19",
  "verbatim_typos_preserved": [
   "`Blaphemous` is printed that way on the wiki (for Blasphemous).",
   "`Rebellious` lists `holy Blast` with a lowercase h.",
   "Both are kept as printed. Correcting a source in its own shard is how a harvest stops being a harvest; the join that consumes this may fold case, and `docs/solutions/` records why silent corrections are refused."
  ],
  "slot_vocabulary": "The `slot` column uses SINGULAR names (Weapon, Ring, Armor, Shield, Orb, ...) and is a THIRD vocabulary, matching neither table 1b's plural groups (`Melee weapons`, `Rings`) nor the app's own slot list. `Weapon` here is undifferentiated - it does not split Melee from Ranged. Joining it is deliberately not done in this file.",
  "minimum_level": "The page states ML 20 for both waves: Update 81 introduced 100 more combined shards 'with a minimum level of 20', and 'The old U55 shards now have both Unbound and Bound crafting recipes and are also now ML20.' The table itself carries no ML column, so the floor is prose-sourced, not per-row.",
  "columns": {
   "name": "the shard's prefix name as it appears on the item",
   "effect_1": "first granted effect, verbatim",
   "effect_2": "second granted effect, verbatim",
   "mystical_cost": "mystical ingredient cost; '-' where the page prints none",
   "slots": "item kinds the shard may be crafted onto, split from the page's comma list",
   "update": "the update that introduced the shard (55 or 81)",
   "bound_level": "crafting level for the bound recipe",
   "unbound_level": "crafting level for the unbound recipe"
  }
 },
